 "cells": [
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": "\n# GeoFedMask: reproducible federated-learning experiments\The accompanying `geofedmask_experiments.py` implements the missing experiments: training-fold-only preprocessing with 35 candidate features and SelectKBest-25; IID, geographic, and label-skew controls; FedAvg, FedProx, IFCA, weighted/unweighted geographic clustered FL, random clusters, and local-only training; five coordinate masks; AIE, Re-ID@100m, ARI, accuracy, macro-F1, AUC, and a loss-based MIA summary; ablation, sensitivity, confidence intervals, and matched-seed tests.\n\n## Important boundary\n\nThe uploaded daily input uses an ECDC-style schema, not an immutable JHU CSSE snapshot. The notebook writes the observed sample count, feature count, selected features, input hashes, and protocol into `outputs/manifest.json`. Do not claim 23,850 instances, 35 usable candidates, or any specific performance value unless the saved manifest and per-seed CSV files show it.\n\n`planar_laplace` is implemented as coordinate perturbation; this notebook does not claim a global formal geo-indistinguishability guarantee. The location evaluation covers only location-derived client coordination metadata against a declared nearest-candidate attacker. 
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": "\n# In a fresh environment, install once before running this notebook:\n# %pip install -r requirements.txt\n\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport json\nimport os\nimport pandas as pd\nimport matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n\nfrom geofedmask_experiments import (\n    ProtocolConfig,\n    load_raw_data,\n    run_smoke_test,\n    main_comparison,\n    privacy_utility_experiment,\n    ablation_experiment,\n    sensitivity_experiment,\n    write_artifacts,\n)\n\nprint(\"Imported reproducible GeoFedMask experiment module.\")\n",
   "execution_count": null,
   "outputs": []
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": "\n## 1. Paths and protocol\n\nThe notebook uses repository-relative paths. Use the following GitHub layout:\n\n```text\nGeoFedMask_reproducible_experiments.ipynb\ngeofedmask_experiments.py\nrequirements.txt\ndata/raw/daily.csv\ndata/raw/static_metadata.csv\n```\n\nRun the smoke test first. The full 15-seed grid can take substantial CPU time.\n"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": "\nPROJECT_ROOT = Path.cwd().resolve()\nDAILY_CSV = Path(os.environ.get(\"GEOFEDMASK_DAILY_CSV\", PROJECT_ROOT / \"data/raw/daily.csv\"))\nSTATIC_CSV = Path(os.environ.get(\"GEOFEDMASK_STATIC_CSV\", PROJECT_ROOT / \"data/raw/static_metadata.csv\"))\nOUTPUT_DIR = PROJECT_ROOT / \"outputs\"\nRUN_FULL_PROTOCOL = False\n\n# Reportable settings; do not tune these against test metrics.\nprotocol = ProtocolConfig(\n    rounds=25,\n    local_epochs=5,\n    learning_rate=0.001,\n    weight_decay=0.0001,\n    train_batch_size=64,\n    eval_batch_size=128,\n    n_clusters=3,\n    fedprox_mu=0.01,\n    label_skew_alpha=0.30,\n    candidate_features=35,\n    selected_features=25,\n    primary_mask=\"planar_laplace\",\n    primary_mask_scale_km=1.0,\n    mask_scales_km=(0.25, 0.50, 1.00, 2.00),\n    reid_threshold_km=0.10,\n    seeds=tuple(range(1, 16)),\n    client_counts=(8, 10, 15),\n)\n\nprint(f\"Daily input: {DAILY_CSV}\")\nprint(f\"Static input: {STATIC_CSV}\")\nassert DAILY_CSV.exists(), \"Set GEOFEDMASK_DAILY_CSV or add data/raw/daily.csv.\"\nassert STATIC_CSV.exists(), \"Set GEOFEDMASK_STATIC_CSV or add data/raw/static_metadata.csv.\"\n",
   "execution_count": null,
   "outputs": []
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": "\n## 2. Data and supervised-task audit\n\nThe label is 1 if next-day 14-day incidence per 100,000 exceeds the current value. Future target information is not a feature. Source countries act as *simulated clients* constructed from aligned country time series; this does not claim that they are independently collected organizations. All input and feature facts printed here are copied to the manifest.\n"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": "\nraw = load_raw_data(DAILY_CSV, STATIC_CSV)\nprint(json.dumps(raw.metadata, indent=2))\n\nif raw.metadata[\"candidate_feature_count\"] < protocol.selected_features:\n    raise RuntimeError(\"The supplied data cannot support SelectKBest-25.\")\nif raw.metadata[\"candidate_feature_count\"] != protocol.candidate_features:\n    print(\"WARNING: report the observed candidate count from the manifest, not the configured target.\")\n",
   "execution_count": null,
   "outputs": []
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": "\n## 3. Smoke test\n\nThis uses one seed, eight geographic clients, two rounds, and one local epoch. It verifies the full code path but is **not** a reportable result.\n"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": "\nsmoke_paths = run_smoke_test(raw, OUTPUT_DIR / \"smoke\")\nfor label, path in smoke_paths.items():\n    print(f\"{label}: {path}\")\n\nsmoke = pd.read_csv(OUTPUT_DIR / \"smoke\" / \"main_smoke_seed_results.csv\")\nsmoke[[\"method\", \"test_accuracy\", \"test_macro_f1\", \"test_auc\", \"mia_loss_auc\", \"aie_km\", \"reid_at_100m_percent\", \"cluster_ari\"]]\n",
   "execution_count": null,
   "outputs": []
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": "\n## 4. Full experiment grid\n\nSetting `RUN_FULL_PROTOCOL = True` runs the missing experiments and writes raw seed-level results before aggregation:\n\n1. **Main comparison:** FedAvg, FedProx, IFCA, weighted unmasked geographic clustering, and GeoFedMask under IID, geographic, and label-skew partitions for \\(N\\in\\{8,10,15\\}\\).\n2. **Privacy--utility:** five masks at four prespecified scales, with every other GeoFedMask setting held fixed.\n3. **Ablation:** FedAvg, random clusters, unweighted k-means, weighted masked clusters, unmasked oracle, and local-only training.\n4. **Sensitivity:** \\(K\\in\\{2,3,5\\}\\) and \\(N\\in\\{8,15,30\\}\\).\n\n### PMF note\n\nPMF is deliberately not misimplemented. The cited PMF method assumes a mobility model with a location-embedding risky module, group optimisation, and a personal adaptor. This tabular binary model has none of these components. Remove the PMF manuscript row or provide a separately justified, task-faithful PMF adaptation before adding it to this code.\n"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": "\nif RUN_FULL_PROTOCOL:\n    main_seed = main_comparison(raw, OUTPUT_DIR, protocol, partitions=(\"iid\", \"geographic\", \"label_skew\"))\n    privacy_seed = privacy_utility_experiment(raw, OUTPUT_DIR, protocol, n_clients=15, partition=\"geographic\")\n    ablation_seed = ablation_experiment(raw, OUTPUT_DIR, protocol, n_clients=15, partition=\"geographic\")\n    sensitivity_seed = sensitivity_experiment(\n        raw, OUTPUT_DIR, protocol,\n        client_counts=(8, 15, 30),\n        cluster_counts=(2, 3, 5),\n        partition=\"geographic\",\n    )\n    artifacts = write_artifacts(\n        OUTPUT_DIR,\n        raw,\n        protocol,\n        {\n            \"main\": main_seed,\n            \"privacy_utility\": privacy_seed,\n            \"ablation\": ablation_seed,\n            \"sensitivity\": sensitivity_seed,\n        },\n    )\n    for label, path in artifacts.items():\n        print(f\"{label}: {path}\")\nelse:\n    print(\"Full protocol skipped. Set RUN_FULL_PROTOCOL = True only after finalizing the data snapshot and compute budget.\")\n",
   "execution_count": null,
   "outputs": []
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": "\n## 5. Results summaries and figures\n\nThe following uses only saved seed-level output, ensuring the figures cannot diverge from the data used for summary tables. It deliberately does not turn smoke-test results into manuscript figures.\n"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": "\nif RUN_FULL_PROTOCOL:\n    main_summary = pd.read_csv(OUTPUT_DIR / \"main_summary.csv\")\n    privacy_summary = pd.read_csv(OUTPUT_DIR / \"privacy_utility_summary.csv\")\n    ablation_summary = pd.read_csv(OUTPUT_DIR / \"ablation_summary.csv\")\n    sensitivity_summary = pd.read_csv(OUTPUT_DIR / \"sensitivity_summary.csv\")\n    paired_tests = pd.read_csv(OUTPUT_DIR / \"main_paired_tests.csv\")\n\n    display(main_summary)\n    display(paired_tests)\n\n    # Privacy--utility curves, one curve per mask, mean of matched seeds.\n    fig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(7.0, 4.2))\n    for mask, group in privacy_summary.dropna(subset=[\"aie_km_mean\", \"test_accuracy_mean\"]).groupby(\"mask\", sort=True):\n        group = group.sort_values(\"aie_km_mean\")\n        ax.plot(group[\"aie_km_mean\"], group[\"test_accuracy_mean\"], marker=\"o\", linewidth=1.4, label=mask.replace(\"_\", \" \"))\n    ax.set_xlabel(\"Average inference error, AIE (km; higher is better privacy)\")\n    ax.set_ylabel(\"Predictive accuracy (%)\")\n    ax.grid(True, linestyle=\":\", linewidth=0.6)\n    ax.legend(frameon=False, fontsize=8)\n    fig.tight_layout()\n    fig.savefig(OUTPUT_DIR / \"privacy_utility_tradeoff.pdf\", bbox_inches=\"tight\")\n    plt.show()\n\n    # Component ablation with saved 95% CI error bars.\n    plot = ablation_summary.dropna(subset=[\"test_accuracy_mean\"])\n    fig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(7.0, 4.2))\n    ax.bar(plot[\"method\"], plot[\"test_accuracy_mean\"], yerr=plot.get(\"test_accuracy_ci95_halfwidth\"), color=\"#4C78A8\", edgecolor=\"black\", linewidth=0.6, capsize=3)\n    ax.set_ylabel(\"Predictive accuracy (%)\")\n    ax.tick_params(axis=\"x\", rotation=30)\n    ax.grid(axis=\"y\", linestyle=\":\", linewidth=0.6)\n    fig.tight_layout()\n    fig.savefig(OUTPUT_DIR / \"component_ablation.pdf\", bbox_inches=\"tight\")\n    plt.show()\n\n    # K-sensitivity with saved 95% CI error bars.\n    fig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(6.5, 4.2))\n    for n_clients, group in sensitivity_summary.groupby(\"n_clients\", sort=True):\n        group = group.sort_values(\"k\")\n        ax.errorbar(group[\"k\"], group[\"test_accuracy_mean\"], yerr=group.get(\"test_accuracy_ci95_halfwidth\"), marker=\"o\", capsize=3, label=f\"N = {n_clients}\")\n    ax.set_xlabel(\"Number of geographic clusters, K\")\n    ax.set_ylabel(\"Predictive accuracy (%)\")\n    ax.set_xticks([2, 3, 5])\n    ax.grid(True, linestyle=\":\", linewidth=0.6)\n    ax.legend(frameon=False)\n    fig.tight_layout()\n    fig.savefig(OUTPUT_DIR / \"k_sensitivity.pdf\", bbox_inches=\"tight\")\n    plt.show()\nelse:\n    print(\"Run the full protocol first; this cell intentionally does not plot smoke-test values.\")\n",
   "execution_count": null,
   "outputs": []
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": "\n## 6. Reporting checklist\n\nBefore adding results to the manuscript, verify the source checksums, actual row count, usable candidate count, selected features, seeds, client counts, and protocol in `outputs/manifest.json`. Use the per-seed CSVs for every table value. `main_paired_tests.csv` contains matched-seed mean differences, confidence intervals, and Holm--Bonferroni-adjusted p-values.\n\nNever replace generated values with manually chosen values. If a manifest property conflicts with the manuscript, correct the claim or rerun the documented protocol with the appropriate raw data.\n"
  }
 ]
}
